Category: security
Summary: read the user overrides file from %USERPROFILE%\.remilia\ instead of LibreWolf's .librewolf folder

Purpose: LibreWolf's profile-directory.patch makes AutoConfig load
librewolf.overrides.cfg from %USERPROFILE%\.librewolf\ on Windows (the branch
without XDG support). With that path, overrides written for an installed
LibreWolf would also change Remilia's prefs, including security and privacy
prefs. Remilia reads only %USERPROFILE%\.remilia\librewolf.overrides.cfg.
Files: extensions/pref/autoconfig/src/prefcalls.js (Windows/non-XDG branch).
The file name stays librewolf.overrides.cfg: it is internal to the AutoConfig
mechanism, like librewolf.cfg. The Linux XDG and legacy branches are not
changed (Linux is not a Remilia target).
Prefs touched: the default of autoadmin.global_config_url, computed at startup.
Upstreamable: no (Remilia identity).
Reverting: Remilia reads LibreWolf's overrides file again.

--- a/extensions/pref/autoconfig/src/prefcalls.js
+++ b/extensions/pref/autoconfig/src/prefcalls.js
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@
       if ((profile_directory = Services.env.get("USERPROFILE") || Services.env.get("HOME"))) {
         defaults.setCharPref(
           "autoadmin.global_config_url",
-          `file://${profile_directory}/.librewolf/librewolf.overrides.cfg`
+          `file://${profile_directory}/.remilia/librewolf.overrides.cfg`
         );
       }
     }
